ession. Ex:'k&(!a|b)'.\n      Default: k\n    --no-alpha-renaming\n      Do not alpha rename anonymous variables in output.\n      Default: false\n    --no-sort-collections\n      Do not sort collections before printing (for speed).\n      Default: false\n    --no-substitution-filtering\n      Do not remove conjuncts of anonymous variables from substitution in \n      output. \n      Default: false\n    --output <mode>, -o <mode>\n      How to display krun results. <mode> is either \n      [pretty|program|kast|binary|json|kore|none]. \n      Default: PRETTY\n      Possible Values: [PRETTY, PROGRAM, KAST, JSON, KORE, NONE]\n    --output-file <file>\n      Store output in the file instead of displaying it.\n    --output-flatten <KLabels>\n      (Assoc) KLabels to flatten into one list.\n      Default: []\n    --output-omit <KLabels>\n      KLabels to omit from the output.\n      Default: []\n    --output-tokast <KLabels>\n      KLabels to output as KAST tokens.\n      Default: []\n    --output-tokenize <KLabels>\n      KLabels to tokenize underneath (reducing output size).\n      Default: []\n    --spec-module <name>, -sm <name>\n      Name of module containing specification to prove\n    --temp-dir <path>\n      Put temp files in this location. Default is /tmp/.<tool>-xxx\n    --trusted <labels>\n      Mark this comma separated list of claims as [trusted]\n    --verbose, -v\n      Print verbose output messages\n      Default: false\n    --version\n      Print version information\n      Default: false\n    --warnings <level>, -w <level>\n      Warning level. Values: [all|normal|none]\n      Default: NORMAL\n      Possible Values: [ALL, NORMAL, NONE]\n    --warnings-to-errors, -w2e\n      Convert warnings to errors.\n      Default: false\n    -I <path>\n      Add a directory to the search path for requires statements.\n      Default: []\n    -W <warning>\n      Enable specific warning categories. Values: [non-exhaustive-match|undeleted-temp-dir|missing-hook-java|missing-syntax-module|invalid-exit-code|deprecated-backend|invalid-config-var|future-error|unused-var|proof-lint|useless-rule|unresolved-function-symbol|malformed-markdown|invalidated-cache|unused-symbol|removed-anywhere]\n      Default: []\n    -Wno <warning>\n      Disable specific warning categories.\n      Default: []\n\n"}]
